[<s>Gautama Buddha</s> — 7 synonyms]
(1.1.29) He is <s>Śākyasiṃha</s> (lion of the Śākyas), <s>Sarvārthasiddha</s> (fulfiller of all goals), and <s>Śauddhodani</s> (son of Śuddhodana);
(1.1.30) and <s>Gautama</s>, and <s>Arkabandhu</s> (kinsman of the sun), and son of <s>Māyādevī</s>.

[<s>Kṛṣṇa</s>'s bow, mark, horses]
(1.1.67) The bow of <s>Murāri</s> (foe of Mura) is <s>Śārṅga</s>; <s>Śrīvatsa</s> is known as his mark;
(1.1.68) and the horses are <s>Śaivya</s> and others.

## Meteor (1), Ash (5), Forest fire (3) ##
(1.1.134) <s>Ulkā</s> is a firebrand with a projecting flame. <s>Bhūti</s>, <s>bhasita</s>, and <s>bhasman</s> [are synonyms for ash];
(1.1.135) <s>kṣāra</s> (alkaline ash) and <s>rakṣā</s> (protective ash) also [mean ash]. But <s>dāva</s>, <s>dava</s>, and <s>vanahutāśana</s> [mean] forest fire.

## Ray (11 synonyms), Light or brightness (11 synonyms), Sunlight (3 synonyms) ##
(1.3.245) <s>Kiraṇa</s>, <s>Usra</s>, <s>Mayūkha</s>, <s>Aṃśu</s>, <s>Gabhasti</s>, <s>Ghṛṇi</s>, <s>Raśmi</s> [are synonyms for ray];
(1.3.246) <s>Bhānu</s>, <s>Kara</s>, <s>Marīci</s> (feminine); <s>Dīdhiti</s> (feminine) [is used] in both masculine and feminine.
(1.3.247) <s>Prabhā</s>, <s>Ruc</s>, <s>Tviṣ</s>, <s>Bhā</s>, <s>Chavi</s>, <s>Dyuti</s>, <s>Dīpti</s> [are synonyms for light/brightness];
(1.3.248) <s>Rocis</s>, <s>Śocis</s> — both neuter; <s>Prakāśa</s>, <s>Dyota</s>, <s>Ātapa</s> [are synonyms for sunlight].

## Three laughs: loud articulated (1 synonym), smile (1 synonym), laugh (1 synonym), Thrill/goosebumps (2 synonyms) ##
(1.7.477) <s>Ācchuritaka</s> is laughter with a start; that which is slight is <s>smita</s> (smile);
(1.7.478) the middling [laugh] is <s>vihasita</s>; <s>romāñca</s> and <s>romaharṣaṇa</s> [mean thrilling/goosebumps].

## Pain or suffering of various types (9) ##
(1.9.516) '<s>Pīḍā</s>' (oppression), '<s>bādhā</s>' (affliction), '<s>vyathā</s>' (distress), '<s>duḥkha</s>' (suffering), '<s>āmanasya</s>' (mental anguish) — [the last is] born of sorrow;
(1.9.517) '<s>kaṣṭa</s>' (hardship), '<s>kṛcchra</s>' (difficulty), '<s>ābhīla</s>' (terrible) — [used] in all three genders; of these, that which admits of degrees [is the applicable usage].
